# Compose Files

## Project directory

Compose resolves the **project directory** from the first sticky
`COMPOSE_FILE` entry (Compose v2/v5 behavior). Relative `env_file`, volume, and
include paths are rooted there.

- Lead `COMPOSE_FILE` with a **name-only anchor** at the intended project root
  (for example `compose.yaml` with `name:` and no services) when overlays live
  in subfolders.
- Do **not** put a nested path first if env/config files live at the parent
  root — Compose will look for them under the nested directory and fail.
- Prefer running from the project directory (`cd` there) so sticky `.env`
  loads; use `--project-directory` only when you cannot change cwd.

## Overlays and merge

- Base + additive overlays beats duplicated full stacks.
- Keep optional workers/sidecars as overlays or profiles — not forever-on
  services in the base file unless that is the intentional default.
- Document the sticky `COMPOSE_FILE=` contract in the stack README; do not leave
  operators guessing merge order.

## Env and secrets

- Prefer gitignored `.env` / `.config` for host secrets; ship `.env.example`
  with blank placeholders only.
- Never invent service, network, or volume names — read the merged config.
- Relative `env_file:` paths must resolve from the project directory above.
